Journey: Expected premium from the published rating rules
Id: expected-premium
Tags: @library
Description: The rating rules of the Larkspur underwriting manual as expressions; callers compare the app against it.
Params: product, sumInsured, region, riskAge, noClaimsYears
Returns: base, regionFactor, loadingPct, loaded, ncdPct, discount, net, tax, total

Set variable rate to product == "HOME" ? 0.0025 : 0.035
Set variable regionFactor to region == "NORTH" ? 1 : region == "SOUTH" ? 1.1 : region == "COAST" ? 1.25 : 1.15
If product == "HOME" then
  Set variable loadingPct to number(riskAge) > 30 ? 12 : 0
Otherwise
  Set variable loadingPct to number(riskAge) < 25 ? 30 : 0
End
Set variable ncdPct to min(number(noClaimsYears), 5) * 5
Set variable base to round(number(sumInsured) * rate, 2)
Set variable loaded to round(base * regionFactor * (1 + loadingPct / 100), 2)
Set variable discount to round(loaded * ncdPct / 100, 2)
Set variable net to max(150, round(loaded - discount, 2))
Set variable tax to round(net * number(TAX_RATE), 2)
Set variable total to round(net + tax, 2)
